From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/22] usb2otg: do not name ARM instructions in a portable driver

The BCM2708 USB OTG driver is portable C everywhere else: its register
accessors go through dmb() from <asm/cpu.h>, and its MMIO is
byte-order-correct because arm-native supports armeb. It also wrote
asm volatile("yield") in twenty-five places and asm volatile("dsb sy") in
two, which are ARM mnemonics and stop the file assembling anywhere else.

Behind USB2OTG_RELAX() and USB2OTG_DSB() the ARM builds are unchanged --
the same instructions, guarded by __arm__/__aarch64__ -- and the driver
builds for a target that is not ARM. This is not hypothetical: AROS/m68k
runs on the same Raspberry Pi silicon under Emu68.
---
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intern.h | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_core.c | 6 +++---
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_device.c | 2 +-
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intr.c | 28 ++++++++++++++--------------
 arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_schedule.c | 14 +++++++-------
 5 files changed

diff --git a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intern.h b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intern.h
index 10e1ce0247..1f75977498 100644
--- a/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intern.h
+++ b/arch/arm-native/soc/broadcom/2708/usb/usb2otg/usb2otg_intern.h
@@ -107,13 +107,38 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * A spin-loop hint and a data barrier, without naming one CPU's instructions.
+ *
+ * This driver is otherwise portable C. Its register accessors already go
+ * through dmb() from <asm/cpu.h>, and its MMIO is byte-order-correct because
+ * arm-native supports armeb -- but it also wrote asm volatile("yield") and
+ * asm volatile("dsb sy") inline in twenty-nine places, which are ARM mnemonics
+ * and stop the file assembling anywhere else.
+ *
+ * The BCM2708 is not only ever driven from an ARM core: AROS/m68k runs on the
+ * same silicon under Emu68, and with these behind a macro the driver builds
+ * there unmodified.
+ *
+ * YIELD is a hint to a multithreaded core that the thread is spinning. It has
+ * no architectural effect, and elsewhere it becomes the compiler barrier that
+ * the surrounding poll loops actually depend on.
+ */
+#if defined(__arm__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+#define USB2OTG_RELAX()     asm volatile("yield\n")
+#define USB2OTG_DSB()       asm volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory")
+#else
+#define USB2OTG_RELAX()     asm volatile("" ::: "memory")
+#define USB2OTG_DSB()       dsb()
+#endif
+
+/*
  * Spin-wait for AHB master IDLE (RESET[31]). Required by DWC2 spec
  * before any soft reset or FIFO flush.
  */
 static inline BOOL usb2otg_wait_ahb_idle(int timeout, const char *where)
 {
     while (!(rd32le(USB2OTG_RESET) & USB2OTG_RESET_AHBIDLE) && --timeout > 0)
-        asm volatile("yield\n");
+        USB2OTG_RELAX();
     if (timeout <= 0)
     {
         bug("[USB2OTG] AHB IDLE wait timed out (%s)\n", where);
@@ -127,7 +152,7 @@
     const char *what)
 {
     while ((rd32le(USB2OTG_RESET) & bit) && --timeout > 0)
-        asm volatile("yield\n");
+        USB2OTG_RELAX();
     if (timeout <= 0)
     {
         bug("[USB2OTG] %s timed out\n", what);
